            {
                "entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                "word": "instalator",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "pl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                        "entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                        "glosses": [
                            "osoba zakładająca instalację"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba54db0e-94da-4f4b-a243-0da639c18fb5",
                                "sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                                "text": "W procesie projektowania architekt musi współpracować z konstruktorami i instalatorami."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f20ad84a-2a15-4113-be70-c3b0d2e7a9bc",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                        "target_lang_word": "installer",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "installer",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2aa16a1f-25ff-34e4-8d91-8c78a7b188e0",
                                        "entry_id": "44420972-2831-35a6-834d-395ca8f5f568",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who installs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8caf14d5-085d-4d83-8d2d-bb72d146e1d1",
                                                "sense_id": "2aa16a1f-25ff-34e4-8d91-8c78a7b188e0",
                                                "text": "In the event industry there are two critical times when safety is often compromised, at bump-in and at bump-out. At bump-in the organizer is usually pressed for time and it is not uncommon for installers to work around the clock. At the end of the show or exhibition, bump-out carries an even higher risk as everyone is exhausted."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bee75300-c0ae-320b-9f39-03a99d1d0b48",
                                        "entry_id": "44420972-2831-35a6-834d-395ca8f5f568",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A program that installs software in a computer and prepares it for use."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad802074-24c7-4c00-aa4c-d02e167b48c8",
                                                "sense_id": "bee75300-c0ae-320b-9f39-03a99d1d0b48",
                                                "text": "Because this version of the Windows Installer is aware of the GAC, it has the capability to publish components into it. […] You can manually or programmatically push an assembly into the GAC by using the command-line tool Gacutil.exe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e7720f0-e6a5-4ec1-ae6b-627ef530b0d3",
                                                "sense_id": "bee75300-c0ae-320b-9f39-03a99d1d0b48",
                                                "text": "Slackware does not include a graphical installer. Its package manager does not perform any dependency resolution. This can be jarring for new users, particularly within the last few years, but it also enables a deeper understanding of the system."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a6bbfae3-2731-4a5a-b135-84a3d4ca9f20",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                        "target_lang_word": "fitter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "fitter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4308407b-2e17-3fc4-b387-834bdb9df78c",
                                        "entry_id": "e6f52add-effa-331c-a36a-e7ddac136a47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who fits or assembles something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3056a9f1-5b1b-4d0b-951a-c37f8e47b1e4",
                                                "sense_id": "4308407b-2e17-3fc4-b387-834bdb9df78c",
                                                "text": "a fitter of clothing, or of machinery"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9d8a2778-1542-4605-8fb8-b2cbf1bb5146",
                                                "sense_id": "4308407b-2e17-3fc4-b387-834bdb9df78c",
                                                "text": "But in the early days of the scheme the new machines created some problems for the fitters, who found them over-complex and their faults hard to diagnose after many years' experience of small, simple steam locomotives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02d8dbc3-c3cb-4ea8-838b-2d9fffb3f3a5",
                                                "sense_id": "4308407b-2e17-3fc4-b387-834bdb9df78c",
                                                "text": "\"They have gone past their sell-by date. But the fitters have done an amazing job keeping these units running for as long as they have."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4a8a104-65a8-30e2-ad5e-0b0c02fc19c0",
                                        "entry_id": "e6f52add-effa-331c-a36a-e7ddac136a47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An epileptic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5325488-3763-3364-b681-083e43dc0235",
                                        "entry_id": "e6f52add-effa-331c-a36a-e7ddac136a47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coal broker who conducts the sales between the owner of a coal pit and the shipper."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "641e752c-bbf4-3566-baee-b7f3688ee38d",
                                        "entry_id": "e6f52add-effa-331c-a36a-e7ddac136a47",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person employed to find suitable music to accompany silent films."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5dfb633a-6426-4ce9-af49-96181539991e",
                                                "sense_id": "641e752c-bbf4-3566-baee-b7f3688ee38d",
                                                "text": "For the fitter of film music in the silent era visual reference was the surest indicator of content."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "fitter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c46a4478-fbaa-3243-b96e-1382201d0e6e",
                                        "entry_id": "57fd0d88-80ee-3857-8b3c-714847da696a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "comparative form of fit: more fit"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "comparative",
                                            "form-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "856f6f4a-17da-4058-87b9-bb980dd4b26c",
                                                "sense_id": "c46a4478-fbaa-3243-b96e-1382201d0e6e",
                                                "text": "An exercise bike won't make you fitter if you never find time to use it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "731574fa-3bfa-45dc-9169-1922f26b946e",
                                                "sense_id": "c46a4478-fbaa-3243-b96e-1382201d0e6e",
                                                "text": "My bird's loads fitter than yours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14b6adc9-dfd9-423b-9964-6729c3583f62",
                                                "sense_id": "c46a4478-fbaa-3243-b96e-1382201d0e6e",
                                                "text": "All stood together on the deck, / For a charnel-dungeon fitter: / All fixed on me their stony eyes, / That in the Moon did glitter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2bc6d025-5d1f-417f-baf7-87cabb09151f",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                        "target_lang_word": "plumber",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plumber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b1ee50d5-4b95-3d29-93b1-01acb4bb9af2",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who works in or with lead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50d05570-1cbe-3712-b79e-58268fb39cb6",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who furnishes, fits, and repairs pipes and other apparatus for the conveyance of water, gas, or drainage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e46628c-f266-3731-a6cb-bf7e5511164c",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who furnishes, fits, and repairs pipes and other apparatus for the conveyance of water, gas, or drainage.",
                                            "One who installs piping for potable and waste water."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "560b75bb-5f79-36af-8138-6ac3217f1b3c",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who investigates or prevents leaks of information."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2dde071-7fe8-4965-a58a-c300f47f4076",
                                                "sense_id": "560b75bb-5f79-36af-8138-6ac3217f1b3c",
                                                "text": "It involved the break-in of the office of Mr. Lewis Fielding, Daniel Ellsberg's psychiatrist, by the White House “plumbers.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4147ab07-40ad-3a2e-9087-2df502ab49d4",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the Royal Navy, an apprentice, a boy aged 16 to 18, who is trained in technical skills at the Dockyard Schools to become an artificer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "551de705-b994-3455-840a-02809f9cdaff",
                                        "entry_id": "64370910-e5e5-39c4-8a02-cbeacd3f90df",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A urologist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97849a34-8d22-4111-b59e-c645c784304a",
                                                "sense_id": "551de705-b994-3455-840a-02809f9cdaff",
                                                "text": "[…] began the month with an operation at St. Joseph Hospital in Aurora, Ill. His surgeon, by the way, was a \"plumber” – urologist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e3ad1d1-7a3c-4cb1-939a-5b0d99bb3fed",
                                                "sense_id": "551de705-b994-3455-840a-02809f9cdaff",
                                                "text": "Within surgery, the \"cleaner\" specialties, such as cardiac and neurosurgery, outrank the plumbers (urologists) and proctologists."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plumber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38691059-ac27-3591-8aab-12b1aa752664",
                                        "entry_id": "5e605028-e570-3e59-b0cd-6c15109e73fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To botch or ruin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6a28221-4bfa-414a-bd06-bc265a159db0",
                                                "sense_id": "38691059-ac27-3591-8aab-12b1aa752664",
                                                "text": "There is nothing to work him into a fine feeling of agony and despair like an exam scheduled for the next day, or a paper to write, or a concert in which he is to sing. Wish him the top of the morning when he is looking forward to one of these events, and then hear the woeful story of how badly he is going to be plumbered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20f3aff7-a1f6-467a-b372-223c6855463c",
                                                "sense_id": "38691059-ac27-3591-8aab-12b1aa752664",
                                                "text": "And yet she sent back his letters unopened and crashed down the telephone receiver on him with monotonous regularity. Well, he guessed it was his own fault. He’d plumbered the works beyond repair that first day."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "000ba4d7-4a89-464a-91a2-945d2ffa4618",
                                                "sense_id": "38691059-ac27-3591-8aab-12b1aa752664",
                                                "text": "If it was not east of where I had started out, I had plumbered myself sure enough, because I didn’t have the energy to go back the other way."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2233b0b-72b7-3c92-b8f9-9a5adf45ebc1",
                                        "entry_id": "5e605028-e570-3e59-b0cd-6c15109e73fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work as a plumber."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dfbe30b8-6eda-4e25-a783-4d4d77f8e558",
                                                "sense_id": "c2233b0b-72b7-3c92-b8f9-9a5adf45ebc1",
                                                "text": "Joe Staudinger plumbered so well that on Saturday night boiling water came from both hot and cold faucets."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1ac6821-f9b9-4883-a5d9-ee715e930a3a",
                                                "sense_id": "c2233b0b-72b7-3c92-b8f9-9a5adf45ebc1",
                                                "text": "Most of us were at the bottom end of the service industry, the ones who plastered or plumbered by day and painted or wrote at night."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1699fe5f-ca5c-4594-becf-e16031849a15",
                                                "sense_id": "c2233b0b-72b7-3c92-b8f9-9a5adf45ebc1",
                                                "text": "[S]he cleaned rich people’s houses—did her work and saved her wages, and Clarence carpentered and plumbered[,] hauled stuff in the old red truck and Ernestine drove to work in a new Datsun."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87b4d829-a410-3655-a763-884e742c3605",
                                        "entry_id": "5e605028-e570-3e59-b0cd-6c15109e73fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To work on (something) as a plumber."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "607dc18b-de51-43e2-8979-b9777f3c4fe5",
                                                "sense_id": "87b4d829-a410-3655-a763-884e742c3605",
                                                "text": "PIPES PLUMBERED BY US stay plumbered till they wear out. No leaky joints or splitting follow our work. How about the pipes on your steam or hot water heater? Don’t they need repacking or perhaps replacing? HAVE US LOOK AT THEM NOW."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f37e767-463d-46b3-9c56-9014c7595bc8",
                                                "sense_id": "87b4d829-a410-3655-a763-884e742c3605",
                                                "text": "Water shows up where no water ever was seen before as the underground water table riseth and runneth over. The surface of the world is a chocolate pudding plumbered by an untutored bride who failed to read the directions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e55c8ce7-f6aa-4b23-bfd2-0991a4ef6683",
                                                "sense_id": "87b4d829-a410-3655-a763-884e742c3605",
                                                "text": "Except that is for the religious ritual of using the washing machine. (These ancient rites had been captured in the brain implant film known as Crease). The ceremony was so tiring, because of the lack of other muscle titillation, that it left the poor peoploids plum tuckered, so that workbots would have to come in to refold the articles of de-hydrated apparel, and somehow get the tucks plumbered, ready for the next service, usually conducted by a fanatical religious leader known as an Engineer."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a26101fd-efc7-3846-888f-543947145a12",
                                        "entry_id": "5e605028-e570-3e59-b0cd-6c15109e73fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To do, work, devise (something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rare",
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0684a28-f09d-40d3-aa1c-10cbbf847019",
                                                "sense_id": "a26101fd-efc7-3846-888f-543947145a12",
                                                "text": "Q. [Mr. Goodman] At the period of time we have spoken of, that strike settled down, did it not, in 1910 and 1911, and there was no strike? A. [Fred C. Schanberger] No. Q. What happened to the Vaudeville Managers’ Co-operative Association’s activities at that time? A. Oh, they kind of plumbered it along and I think I never heard of it so far as I am concerned until this second strike was started."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da0c246a-7476-436b-acff-36083fef9a3d",
                                                "sense_id": "a26101fd-efc7-3846-888f-543947145a12",
                                                "text": "The other afternoon Silly here pilfered a melody from the classics, threw a little jazz at it and I plumbered some words. I got a copy of them with me now. Grab this while it’s hot, Joe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6382257c-36b8-496c-a41a-27f9997e7e97",
                                                "sense_id": "a26101fd-efc7-3846-888f-543947145a12",
                                                "text": "‘My idea!’ Was this bunch of deadwood trying to give him the birdies? ‘Dana—’ / ‘Suppose it was Dana's idea? You are the one that plumbered things.’ / ‘That's right, Duke,’ said Dana, neatly stepping out from under. ‘I merely made a suggestion, You did not have to follow it.’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "abb987ee-6dd0-3f46-ba34-6d063a4b2557",
                                        "entry_id": "5e605028-e570-3e59-b0cd-6c15109e73fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To equip (something) with plumbing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "rare",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c18f4c5e-e570-42d9-99c4-9ae87d03e58a",
                                                "sense_id": "abb987ee-6dd0-3f46-ba34-6d063a4b2557",
                                                "text": "How many times should a bathroom be “plumbered”? IT should be “plumbered” once more if it is an old bathroom of the tin-tub, iron-pipe era. Call in your plumber and have him rip out the old, unsanitary fixtures and the rusting iron or steel pipe and put in modern fixtures connected with good brass pipe that cannot rust. If you are building a new house it should be “plumbered” just once."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7722270a-5e79-4bb1-beb7-169aeadd1e59",
                                                "sense_id": "abb987ee-6dd0-3f46-ba34-6d063a4b2557",
                                                "text": "The silver grey timbers he turned inside out or rather put the weathered side in, heated and plumbered the place and, with his freezing apparatus can live off his chickens, ducks and garden-produce all the year round."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "778a8a61-c1b8-4dd0-bdd0-80a83ed731f9",
                                                "sense_id": "abb987ee-6dd0-3f46-ba34-6d063a4b2557",
                                                "text": "For the most part, they let the land go, perforce; so that nowadays their ancestral mansions gleam spickly and spanly after having been purchased, and lavishly plumbered and electrified, by magnates from out of the North."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "da988a5d-acd2-4d18-9fec-fa77405c0530",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb820624-98e2-3303-8b66-56ab36f65b96",
                        "source_sense_id": "0c10625c-e111-3e3b-b15f-0bbf400386bb",
                        "target_lang_word": "installateur",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "installateur",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a2522c1-199b-3c04-8abb-7a24b9a0ce04",
                                        "entry_id": "a0d6790c-77cf-3a63-a5e6-59bb2acf2ab0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne qui s’occupe d’installation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13a4a119-5379-4a45-8f0b-ece4daca10dc",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2522c1-199b-3c04-8abb-7a24b9a0ce04",
                                                "text": "Le maire de Montreuil institue un « moratoire sur le déploiement des compteurs Linky ». La ville veut suspendre l’installation de ces compteurs controversés par un sous-traitant d’Enedis. Des tensions et des incidents sont survenus entre les installateurs et les habitants ces dernières semaines."
                                            }
                                        ]
